course: dictionary
lesson: 780
title: Beauty: more than looks
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Beauty is a noun with more than one meaning. Most often it means the quality of being very pleasing to look at, hear or think about. «Beauty is in the eye of the beholder» says that different people find different things beautiful.
explain: Use the words around it to choose the right meaning. «Beauty products» and «beauty salon» are about looks, but «the beauty of the plan is that it is cheap» means the best part of the plan. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it makes sense.
explain: Beauty can also be a person or thing, or an informal word for something excellent. «She is a real beauty» means she is very beautiful. «That catch is a beauty!» means it is an excellent catch. In Australia and New Zealand, «you beauty!» is a cheer that means great, well done.
fact: Beauty means the quality of being very pleasing to look at, hear or think about.
fact: «A beauty» can mean a very beautiful person or thing, as in «She is a real beauty».
fact: Informally, «a beauty» means an excellent example of something, as in «That catch is a beauty!».
fact: «Beauty is in the eye of the beholder» means people find different things beautiful.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, «you beauty!» means great, well done.
exercise: «Beauty hides in odd places: the spirals in a sunflower follow a number pattern.» In this sentence, what does beauty mean? | *The quality of being pleasing to look at or think about | A sale on products | A very beautiful person | A salon where people get their hair cut
exercise: Dad says, «That catch is a beauty!» What does a beauty mean here? | A very beautiful person | A place where you buy make-up | *An excellent example of something | A type of fish
exercise: «The beauty of the plan is that it is cheap.» What does beauty mean in this sentence? | A shop that sells products | A very beautiful thing | The quality of looking pretty | *The best or nicest part
test: «Cracks are common in pottery; the Japanese art of kintsugi even repairs broken pots with gold so the cracks become part of the beauty.» In this sentence, beauty means | a very beautiful person | *the quality of being pleasing to look at | an informal word for great | a beauty salon
test: Ruby wins her race and shouts, «you beauty!» What does it mean? | She is sad about losing | She has bought a beauty product | She looks very pretty | *Great, well done
exam: «Beauty is in the eye of the beholder» means | *different people find different things beautiful | everyone finds exactly the same thing beautiful | only experts can decide what is beautiful | beauty is not real
